import{_ as t,o as n,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 284 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Retcon-Ending Risk: Late-Stage Setting Analysis of \\"I Can See Combat Power\\"","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 284 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Retcon-Ending Risk: Late-Stage Setting Analysis of \\"I Can See Combat Power\\"","no":284,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Retcon-Ending","I Can See Combat Power","Late-Stage Settings","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","98-Expanded Setting Recommendation List","90-Glossary"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0284_模块2-唐罗-吃书烂尾风险.md","filePath":"en/0284_模块2-唐罗-吃书烂尾风险.md"}'),a={name:"en/0284_模块2-唐罗-吃书烂尾风险.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,c,u){return n(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-284-tang-luo-decomposition-retcon-ending-risk-late-stage-setting-analysis-of-i-can-see-combat-power" tabindex="-1">Entry 284 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Retcon-Ending Risk: Late-Stage Setting Analysis of &quot;I Can See Combat Power&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-284-tang-luo-decomposition-retcon-ending-risk-late-stage-setting-analysis-of-i-can-see-combat-power" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 284 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Retcon-Ending Risk: Late-Stage Setting Analysis of &quot;I Can See Combat Power&quot;&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 34)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-1-hidden-cause-of-death-for-long-web-novels" tabindex="-1">Introduction: The #1 hidden cause of death for long web novels <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-1-hidden-cause-of-death-for-long-web-novels" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: The #1 hidden cause of death for long web novels&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom requires never retconning, never ending badly. The #1 hidden cause of death for long web novels is not hiatus, but retconning — settings kidnapped by plot convenience, early iron laws casually broken in late stages. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, specially analyzing the retcon risk in late stages of &quot;I Can See Combat Power,&quot; the work where the Tang-Luo system appears. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Retconning-caused energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Early accumulation voided</strong>: numerical ladders, realm rules, world-view iron laws painstakingly built early are broken late. Early foreshadowing, suspense, setup all voided</li><li><strong>Narrative trust overdrawn</strong>: readers discover rules can be broken, no longer trust the author. Once trust is overdrawn, even good late plot cannot redeem</li><li><strong>Combat-power inflation out of control</strong>: retconning&#39;s direct consequence is combat-power inflation. The protagonist gets stronger and stronger, but readers are numb — because strength depends on the author&#39;s mood</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-retconning-perspective" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Retconning Perspective) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-retconning-perspective" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Retconning Perspective)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Narrative regression caused by retconning:</p><ol><li><strong>Iron laws devalued</strong>: early &quot;hundred-year soul rings already scarce&quot;-style iron laws late become &quot;thousand-year soul rings casually picked up.&quot; Iron laws devalued, narrative tension devalues with them</li><li><strong>Realm collapse</strong>: realms carefully delineated early lose binding force late. Who is strong or weak depends entirely on plot needs</li><li><strong>Foreshadowing unfinished</strong>: suspense laid early has no time to resolve late, can only end badly. Readers&#39; expectations are betrayed</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking behind retconning:</p><ul><li><strong>Plot kidnaps setting</strong>: for plot climaxes, the author may tear up any early iron law. This is predation on reader intelligence</li><li><strong>Combat-power inflation</strong>: the protagonist&#39;s strength stretches with plot needs, early &quot;leveling hard-won&quot; is diluted by late &quot;casual breakthrough&quot;</li><li><strong>Settings as tools</strong>: settings are not world-view skeleton, but plot tools. Tools worn out get replaced — this is disrespect to settings themselves</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Retcon Risk Medium</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Never Retcons</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Early iron laws torn late</td><td>Laws first, iron laws not torn</td></tr><tr><td>Combat-power inflation</td><td>Numerical ladder strict, no inflation</td></tr><tr><td>Foreshadowing unfinished</td><td>Alaya remembers all foreshadowing, no bad ending</td></tr><tr><td>Plot kidnaps setting</td><td>Setting self-consistency over plot convenience</td></tr><tr><td>World-view collapse</td><td>Can expand infinitely without collapse</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Tang-Luo system retcon risk rating: <strong>medium</strong>. Its internal rules have not yet shown Douluo-style late padding, nor Shrouding-the-Heavens-style realm collapse; the main risk point is &quot;single-point dependency&quot; — system rules hinge on one person, once plot requires the protagonist to exit, rules cannot continue.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo system early iron laws</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simulate late plot needing &quot;Tang Luo secludes / turns dark / falls&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: which early iron laws are forced to be torn</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: forced-to-tear iron laws concentrate in three places — &quot;top-tier knowledge private,&quot; &quot;racial boundaries,&quot; &quot;single-point adjudication&quot; — fully overlapping the structural analysis of the first 32 entries in this series</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong></li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong></li><li><strong>Risk source</strong>: single-point dependency structure, not the author&#39;s writing skill</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: early accumulation voided by retconning</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: plot kidnaps setting = predation on reader trust</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s risk is single-point dependency, not combat-power inflation</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: retconning first harms the 99% excluded from the protagonist&#39;s halo</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law-first is the precondition for cross-plane narrative</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-discussion-institutional-prevention-of-retcon-risk" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Discussion: Institutional Prevention of Retcon Risk <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-discussion-institutional-prevention-of-retcon-risk" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Discussion: Institutional Prevention of Retcon Risk&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang-Luo system&#39;s late-overturning-early retcon-ending risk roots in the absence of the law-first axiom&#39;s rigid constraint. Heng Yuan Zhou by writing core laws into the charter and having the Alaya Network auto-verify, ensures late any new setting cannot contradict early anchored laws. Once the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s 300 systems are anchored, revision must go through democratic consultation; the author or protagonist is not allowed unilaterally to overturn. The universal equal infinite law as underlying axiom cannot be infringed by any setting change, rooting out retconning space.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;I Can See Combat Power&quot;&#39;s retcon risk is essentially not an author-skill problem, but a Tang-Luo system structural problem — a single-point-dependency system is destined to face the &quot;what to do when the protagonist exits&quot; problem in long late stages. If the author does not want to retcon, he must keep Tang Luo always present; if he keeps him present, he can never let him truly grow — between this dilemma, retconning is almost inevitable. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom exists precisely to root out this dilemma.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · retcon-ending risk described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a> · <a href="./98-扩展设定建议清单.html">98-Expanded Setting Recommendation List</a> · <a href="./90-术语词典.html">90-Glossary</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const p=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{h as __pageData,p as default};
